{{2011–12 SWAC men's basketball standings}}
The '''2011–12 Grambling State Tigers men's basketball team''' represented [[Grambling State University]] in the [[2011–12 NCAA Division I men's basketball season]]. The Tigers, led by third-year head coach [[Robert Washington (basketball)|Robert Washington]], played their home games at the [[Fredrick C. Hobdy Assembly Center]] in [[Grambling, Louisiana]] as members of the [[Southwestern Athletic Conference]] (SWAC). They finished the season 4–24, 4–14 in SWAC play to finish in last place.<ref>{{cite web |title=2011–2012 Men's Basketball Schedule |url=https://gsutigers.com/sports/mens-basketball/schedule/2011-2012 |website=Grambling State University Athletics |accessdate=June 26, 2020}}</ref> The Tigers had received a one-year postseason ban in May 2011 due to poor academic performance and thus failed to quality for the [[2012 SWAC men's basketball tournament|2012 SWAC tournament]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Vangilder |first1=Lenny |title=ULM, Southern, Grambling Get APR-Related Postseason Bans |url=http://www.sportsnola.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=572650&Itemid=578 |website=Sports NOLA |accessdate=June 26, 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120421151405/http://www.sportsnola.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=572650&Itemid=578 |archivedate=April 21, 2012 |url-status=usurped |date=May 24, 2011}}</ref> It was Washington's final season as head coach for the Tigers as he was dismissed on March 19, 2012.<ref>{{cite web |title=Grambling ‘reassigns’ men’s, women’s head coaches |url=https://www.columbian.com/news/2012/mar/19/grambling-reassigns-mens-womens-head-coaches/ |website=The Columbian |accessdate=June 26, 2020 |date=March 19, 2012}}</ref>

